Short:        WebKit web browser for AmigaOS 3.2 (68040+FPU)
Author:       AmiCradle Team
Uploader:     UPLOADER-PLACEHOLDER
Type:         comm/www
Version:      0.8.4
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.2
Distribution: Aminet

GFOpenBrowser is a web browser for AmigaOS 3.2 built on WebKit: WebCore lays
out and draws real web pages, and JavaScriptCore runs their JavaScript with
the Team's 68k template JIT. Pages are fetched with HTTP/2 and https
(GFOpenTLS), pictures are decoded by the system's datatypes, and pages seen
before load from a disk cache.

This is a test version (0.8.4 test, 1 November 2026). Things will still go
wrong; reports are welcome.

Installing
----------
Double-click Install-GFOpenBrowser (the Installer). It checks for AmigaOS 3.2
and a 68040 or 68060 with its FPU, asks where the GFOpenBrowser drawer goes
(about 90 MB; Work: rather than System:), and adds only what is missing or
too old: gfopentls.library 1.2+, gfopencrypto.library 2.1+, json.library, and
the certificates in S:GFOpenTLS. The browser has one engine,
Libs/WebBrowser/WebBrowserEngine in the drawer, which webbrowser.library
starts; it stays there. An older LIBS:WebBrowser/WebBrowserEngine (the
engine, or the small script 0.8.0 and 0.8.1 test put there) is kept as
WebBrowserEngine.before-20261101, and an older version's GFOpenBrowser.engine
in the drawer as GFOpenBrowser.engine.before-20261101. Nothing is deleted. Novice, Intermediate and
Expert levels, pretend mode and the log all work.

From a Shell instead: CD into the GFOpenBrowser drawer and type
Execute Install.

Reboot after installing, then double-click GFOpenBrowser. It also runs from
the drawer as unpacked, before installing, when json.library, GFOpenTLS and
the certificates are already on the Amiga.

Requirements
------------
- AmigaOS 3.2 or newer
- a 68040 or 68060 with its FPU (hard float; not an LC or EC CPU)
- about 120 MB of free Fast RAM
- a TCP/IP stack with bsdsocket.library (GFOpenSocket or another)

Undo
----
Delete the GFOpenBrowser drawer (or, if it was installed over an older one,
rename the *.before-20261101 files in it back). Rename
LIBS:WebBrowser/WebBrowserEngine.before-20261101, if there is one, back to
WebBrowserEngine. Libraries kept as *.before-20261101 in LIBS: can be
renamed back the same way. The Installer's
log in the drawer (Install-GFOpenBrowser.log, or install_log_file when the
Installer is started from a Shell without LOGFILE), lists everything it did.

